1
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:07,400
On the 12th-century Mongolian steppe,

2
00:00:08,066 --> 00:00:09,066
tribes stood divided,

3
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:10,366
locked in endless conflict.

4
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,866
Survival was the only law.

5
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:15,766
In just a few decades,

6
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:18,366
the empire stretched from the Pacific Ocean in the east

7
00:00:18,733 --> 00:00:20,566
to the Danube River basin in the west.

8
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:25,700
Paper, gunpowder, printing, and astronomy spread westward with it,

9
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:29,000
profoundly reshaping global politics and civilization.

10
00:00:29,266 --> 00:00:31,000
He broke through bloodline boundaries,

11
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,466
established the strict Mingghan system,

12
00:00:34,066 --> 00:00:36,933
and forged a highly disciplined cavalry force.

13
00:00:38,966 --> 00:00:41,766
Skilled at absorbing engineering from various civilizations,

14
00:00:41,866 --> 00:00:44,533
fortified city walls were no longer an obstacle.

15
00:00:45,733 --> 00:00:47,300
In 1206 AD,

16
00:00:47,566 --> 00:00:49,566
the Mongol tribes officially unified,

17
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:52,733
and Temüjin was proclaimed Genghis Khan.

18
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:57,366
With extreme mobility using multiple horses per rider and precise flanking,

19
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:00,666
the Mongol cavalry swept across Eurasia.

20
00:01:01,166 --> 00:01:03,800
A vast postal relay network connected East and West,

21
00:01:04,166 --> 00:01:06,066
ushering the Silk Road into

22
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:08,800
an unprecedented era of trade and cultural exchange.

23
00:01:09,766 --> 00:01:11,533
When the sound of hoofbeats faded,

24
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:13,866
he left behind not just an empire,

25
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,000
but a completely reshaped world order.

26
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:20,166
With trust and foresight, he united people's hearts,

27
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:23,100
bringing scattered tribes back together.